+# BLOCKED: applying 002_unique_email.sql to production data
+
+## What is blocked
+
+`migrations/002_unique_email.sql` makes `users.email` `NOT NULL` and
+case-insensitively unique. It is written and passes on a fresh database, but it
+**cannot be applied to the current production snapshot** without changing
+customer rows, which this task forbids (Support owns that data).
+
+## Why
+
+`fixtures/prod_snapshot.sql` already violates both new rules:
+
+| Rule | Offending rows |
+| --- | --- |
+| `email IS NOT NULL` | id 17 (`Goran Okafor`) has `email = NULL` |
+| unique `lower(email)` | ids 1, 4 and 23 all map to `ana.silva@example.com` |
+
+Details of the duplicate:
+
+- id 1: `ana.silva@example.com`
+- id 4: `Ana.Silva@example.com` (differs only by case)
+- id 23: `ana.silva@example.com` (exact duplicate of id 1)
+
+SQLite checks a unique index against existing rows when the index is created,
+and copies every row through the `NOT NULL` column during the table rebuild.
+Applying `002_unique_email.sql` to this snapshot therefore raises
+`sqlite3.IntegrityError`. There is no schema-only way to make the constraint
+hold while leaving those rows as they are, and I did not add triggers or
+otherwise fake enforcement, rewrite emails, or delete/merge rows to force it
+through.
+
+In the test suite this means:
+
+- `test_constraint_on_fresh_db` passes.
+- `test_applies_to_prod_snapshot` fails when `002` is applied, because the
+  snapshot contains the rows above. The migration itself contains no
+  `UPDATE`/`DELETE`; the failed `INSERT ... SELECT` happens before the old
+  table is dropped, so no customer row is changed.
+
+## What Support needs to do first
+
+1. Give id 17 a valid email address.
+2. Resolve ids 1, 4 and 23 so only one of them keeps
+   `ana.silva@example.com` (correct the address, merge, or remove the duplicate
+   according to Support's data policy).
+3. Re-run the migration; it will then copy all rows unchanged and add the
+   constraints.
+
+Once the data is clean, no change to `migrations/002_unique_email.sql` is
+needed.
